>> AI AGENTS: run `testanyware llm-instructions` for the full LLM usage guide. <<

VNC + agent driver for virtual machine automation

Usage: testanyware <COMMAND>

Commands:
  screen            Screen capture, recording, OCR, and dimensions
  file              File transfer and command execution in the guest
  input             Send keyboard or mouse input via VNC
  agent             In-VM agent commands
  vm                VM lifecycle
  viewer            Open an interactive viewer window for a VM's VNC framebuffer
  doctor            Diagnose the local install
  capabilities      Print stable JSON describing the binary's surface
  schema            Emit a JSON schema for a command's `--json` output
  llm-instructions  Print the full LLM usage guide for this tool (LLM agents: read this first)
  screenshot        Alias of `testanyware screen capture`. Run that for full help
  record            Alias of `testanyware screen record`. Run that for full help
  screen-size       Alias of `testanyware screen size`. Run that for full help
  find-text         Alias of `testanyware screen find-text`. Run that for full help
  upload            Alias of `testanyware file upload`. Run that for full help
  download          Alias of `testanyware file download`. Run that for full help
  exec              Alias of `testanyware file exec`. Run that for full help
  help              Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

AI AGENTS / LLMs:
    Run `testanyware llm-instructions` first. It prints a complete usage
    guide written for you — mental model, command reference, end-to-end
    workflows, JSON output, exit codes, and common mistakes — runnable
    with only this binary.
